# Emergency braking (docs/emergency_stop.md) on the burn-in axis (10 mm a
# revolution): at 188 rad/s (300 mm/s) something fails; hv0.sim_dist,
# zeroed then, is how far the axis went (1 rad = 1.59 mm). Coasting takes
# ~16 rad (26 mm) and ~180 ms.
# estop_fb.test with the brake current limited to 2 A (dbrake0.max_cur): rv
# rises and holds the current at the limit within a few ms (the first ms
# carry the current from before the fault); once the short alone stays
# below the limit, rv is back at 0. A resistor brakes harder at
# speed than a short, which the motor's inductance holds back, so it also
# stops sooner; that energy goes to the DC bus.
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 300
run 1
hv0.sim_vel
hv0.sim_dist = 0
dbrake0.max_cur = 2
enc_fb0.sim_fail = 1
run 0.004
@sample dbrake0.rv 0.001 0.006
@sample hv0.abs_cur 0.001 0.008
run 0.25
hv0.sim_dist
hv0.sim_vel
fault0.en_out
@expect max dbrake0.rv > 1
@expect max|hv0.abs_cur| < 2.3
@expect hv0.sim_dist < 2.5
@expect hv0.sim_vel[2] ~ 0 0.5
@expect fault0.en_out == 0
